                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "From the first glance It looks like a very good arkanoid with storymode, startegic economy element, nice visual design & original level architecture (landscapes on floating islands), but after some playtime I had to ragequit this for the bat physics seems terribly off. For example, how'd you like a bat kicking the lonely ball twice in a fracture of a sec? This happens if you move it too fast. It gives a short pass to itself kinda.. If the ball is visually situated over the bat it goes in a random direction. The way the ball & the bat are visualized seems inconsistent with the physics & it's a death sentence to an arkanoid game. You may kick it forward with it's backside or vice versa.\n\nThe ball might get cought in a endless loop of rebounds - in all arkanoids I have played this issue was not possible 'cause the ball's trajectory always got varied a bit, here it's not the case.\n\nYou control the bat with the mouse only & in the most dynamic moments it lags a bit & you lose it from view momentarily. Then it kicks the ball sidewards/backwards. I really can't stand these desyncs, kills the game for me.",
